## Already completed (do NOT re-implement or overwrite)

Session 1 — Project context for Cursor:
- This .cursorrules file exists with Civilian stack constraints.

Session 2 — Shipped in the repo (leave intact unless a task explicitly asks to change that area):
- pages/forum.js: echo localStorage uses echoed_posts only; one-time migration from legacy echoedPosts; 30s polling of /api/posts for the feed.
- pages/index.js: live homepage stats from API + FORUM_THREADS; useCounter handles end <= 0; DemoWidget has inView + 2s fallback and single-start guard (demoStarted ref).
- pages/api/posts.js: GET always returns a JSON array (normalized + fallback posts).
- pages/api/waitlist.js: POST waitlist endpoint (InsForge waitlist table; fail-open if table missing).
- docs/insforge-schema.sql: optional SQL for profiles, echoes, status_history, waitlist, notifications, post columns.
- .env.example: documents real InsForge var names and other keys.
- pages/_document.js: default SEO meta (title, description, og, twitter).

When working on new tasks: do NOT redo the above unless the user explicitly asks to modify those files for a regression or redesign. Prefer extending alongside existing patterns.

---

Rules:
- NEVER use Supabase. The database is InsForge via lib/insforge.js.
- NEVER switch to the App Router. This is Pages Router only.
- NEVER rewrite working files — only modify what the specific task requires.
- ALWAYS use the existing component and lib patterns before creating new ones.
- ALWAYS check what's already imported at the top of a file before adding new imports.
- For auth, use NextAuth with getServerSession on the server and useSession on the client.
- For database queries, follow the pattern already in lib/insforge.js.
- Match the existing Tailwind + Framer Motion animation style.
